#: manual/tutorial/core.md:119
msgid "Going further"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:121
msgid "The package has no traits or types to extend, so going further means treating the greeting as data. Pass `@luna-template.hello` wherever your code needs a `() -> String`, as in `banner` above, and pass a different closure in tests: `banner(() => \"x\")` exercises the same code without the dependency. Calling `hello` costs constant time, so there is no need to cache its result. There is no error handling to do either: `hello` cannot fail."
msgstr ""

